abstract: >-
  shortcut-catcher finds and removes shortcut features: features a model
  exploits on its training data that do not generalise. It ranks the
  features the model relies on with an explainer, retrains without each
  top-ranked candidate, and keeps the removal that scores best on an
  independently collected verification set. Removals accumulate over
  rounds. The algorithm is independent of the data type; the package ships
  a tabular backend (Random Forest with Gini importance) and an
  experimental text backend (frozen ELECTRA encoder).
